 cent from $40.0 trillion for the same period last year.\\n\\n- The average daily turnover in March 2026 was $304.0 billion, an increase of 8 per cent from $280.2 billion for the same period last year.\\n\\n- The average daily turnover for the first three months of 2026 was $276.7 billion, an increase of 14 per cent when compared with $242.7 billion for the same period last year.\\n\\n- The average daily turnover of derivative warrants for the first three months of 2026 was $7.5 billion, an increase of 1 per cent when compared with $7.4 billion for the same period last year.\\n\\n- The average daily turnover of CBBCs for the first three months of 2026 was $13.9 billion, an increase of 40 per cent when compared with $9.9 billion for the same period last year.\\n\\n- The average daily turnover of ETFs for the first three months of 2026 was $40.2 billion, an increase of 15 per cent when compared with $35.0 billion for the same period last year.\\n\\n- The average daily turnover of L&I Products for the first three months of 2026 was $4.9 billion, an increase of 11 per cent when compared with $4.4 billion for the same period last year.\\n\\n- There were 40 newly listed companies for the first three months of 2026, an increase of 135 per cent when compared with 17* for the same period last year.\\n\\n- Funds raised through IPOs# for the first three months of 2026 was $109.9 billion, an increase of 488 per cent when compared with $18.7 billion for the same period last year.\\n\\n- Total funds raised for the first three months of 2026 was $150.2 billion.\\n\\n- Derivatives Market\\n\\n- The average daily volume of futures and options for the first three months of 2026 was 1,828,560 contracts.\\n\\n- The average daily volume of Stock Options for the first three months of 2026 was 943,511 contracts.\\n\\n- On 27 March 2026, the volume of Hang Seng Biotech Index Futures reached a record high of 1,239 contracts.\\n\\n* Includes 1 listing from GEM to Main Board and 1 de-SPAC tra